+## Correction required by N1 — R1 rewritten against the actual balloted text
+
+The balloted §3(1) contains **no** finite "maximum possible loss L", no "signed by Economy" L, and no "new dispatch stops at the ceiling" sentence. The earlier response's R1 asserted all three and said "a finite L remains mandatory". That assertion was false and is withdrawn. The actual text is:
+
+- **R1 (corrected) — tiered, honest ceilings.** §3(1) states ceilings are **accounting and dispatch ceilings, not a mathematical ceiling on tokens billed**, and that the OpenCode 20-second retrospective limiter is **not** a strict per-request cap and must never be labelled as one. §3(1)(a) admits a **zero-billed tier** only where Economy furnishes and independently verifies a runtime/provider model-selection restriction to zero-billed models or an account-level zero-paid-spend cap on the exact dispatch path (a `-free` name is not enforcement; Antonina selects models dynamically); until then the path is HELD. §3(1)(b) admits a **provider-billed tier** only with a provider-enforced hard ceiling independently verified on the exact path; absent that, no provider-billed dispatch and no bounded-loss claim. §3(1)(c) requires per-request input/output ceilings, a continuation multiplier, concurrency/CPU/wall ceilings, a ≤20 s monitor and the cumulative ledger, with the **maximum possible billed overrun reported as a number, never claimed as zero**. §3(2) preserves the non-resettable 45-day `UPPER_BOUND`, cancel/kill and fail-closed wind-down. This is more honest than a nominal L, and it is what the reviewer approved. No "finite L remains mandatory" sentence is retained.
+
+## Point-by-point mapping of the governing findings to the balloted text
+
+- **F1 (adaptive institution vs. fixed telemetry).** §2(2) mandates genuinely adaptive mandates for all four offices (Statistics selects/revises/retires questions; Foresight invents competing trajectories with Act 22-hash-bound forecasts; Strategy investigates expansive trajectories and advises; Spying uses an allowlisted public-source log). §3(3) marks any deterministic/no-provider output `auxiliary_telemetry: true`, never an institution or outcome. The reviewer's final re-review confirmed the mandates remain broad and parallel and that no fixed-report mandate returned (§(d) of the re-review). The adaptive-selection finding at 48 h is carried as an execution condition in the assumptions schedule (C2) and ballot instructions; no prelaunch efficacy gate.
+- **F2 (`model_mode`/independent proof).** §3(1)(a)–(c) is the honest tiered control the reviewer explicitly approved in place of a strict per-request cap: zero-billed admission requires verified runtime/account enforcement, provider-billed admission requires a verified provider-enforced ceiling, and no unbounded-paid-spend route exists. N2 adds the execution negative test (a paid model with a `-free`-looking id must be refused) before any zero-billed model dispatch; this is an execution-verification condition, not a prelaunch efficacy gate, and prescribes no model or provider.
+- **F3 (numeric ceilings, meters, kill).** §3(1)(c) requires per-request, concurrency, CPU/wall ceilings, a ≤20 s monitor and overrun reporting; §3(2) requires cancel/kill and fail-closed wind-down. Numeric aggregate ceilings, unknown-meter blocking and kill-after-billing negative tests are carried as execution conditions in the assumptions schedule (C4) and ballot instructions.
+- **F4 (48 h check anchored).** §4(1) runs the 48 h fail-closed Judiciary review from the permit start, not a later `activation.json` write, and is additional to Act 15 methods. Git-recorded `start_utc` and verifier enforcement are carried as execution conditions (C7).
+- **F5 (authority spillover).** §2(2) binds Spying to the code-enforced allowlist; §3(4) bars Post/confidential-channel spillover and protects Act 15 audits and the Act 21 gate. §7 expressly supersedes the enacted gates that would otherwise deadlock all four.
+- **F6 (assumptions durable).** `records/assumptions/act34-rapid-full-institutional-activation.md` is filed and bound to SHA `6d5f5514…`; the tiered-final Act 31 delivery carries it onto `main` before tally.
+- **F7 (provenance, per-office permits, record integrity).** Provenance cites `sha256:BSTZyiNh…`; §2(1) requires one written, timestamped, reversible permit per office, no permit activates two offices. The misleading `c6a2cbd8` "final bill" landing carried only obsolete minimum-viable files and is expressly superseded by this text.
+- **F8 (express supersession).** §7 names the superseded enacted clauses and preserves Act 32 §§1–8/10–11, Act 33 §1, Act 15 methods and random case selection, Post non-authority, Spying allowlist/secret exclusion, 45-day expiry, cumulative `UPPER_BOUND`, Act 21 gate and the Constitution. The reviewer confirmed F8 is satisfied.
